-- title:
--   Descent of local M-generation along a field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $k'$ be fields with $k'$ a $k$-algebra, let $N, M$ be natural numbers, and let $J$ be an ideal of the polynomial ring $k[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin N) k`. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $k[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]$ with $J \le \mathfrak n$, and let $\mathfrak n'$ be a maximal ideal of $k'[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]$ such that the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak n$ under the coefficientwise map $k[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}] \to k'[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]$ induced by $k \to k'$ is contained in $\mathfrak n'$ (that is, $\mathfrak n'$ lies over $\mathfrak n$). Assume that the ideal generated by the image of $J$ in the localisation $k'[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]_{\mathfrak n'}$ — that is, the extension to this localisation of the ideal generated by the image of $J$ in $k'[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]$ — is the span of the range of some family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,M \to k'[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]_{\mathfrak n'}$. Then the ideal generated by the image of $J$ in $k[x_0,\dots,x_{N-1}]_{\mathfrak n}$ is likewise the span of the range of a family indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,M$. Thus generation by (at most) $M$ elements after localisation descends from $k'$ to $k$; the statement is about the existence of $M$ generators, not about the minimal number of generators being equal.
--
--   This is the descent, along the flat local homomorphism $k[x]_{\mathfrak n} \to k'[x]_{\mathfrak n'}$, of the bound on the number of local generators of an ideal, the underlying mechanism being Nakayama's lemma together with the identification of $J/\mathfrak n J$ after base change to the larger residue field. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_ker_map_localization_eq_span_of_surjective_mvPolynomial_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_ker_map_localization_eq_span_of_surjective_mvPolynomial_of_isMaximal), in the reduction of local complete intersection properties of algebras over a field to the case of an algebraically closed base field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_map_localization_eq_span_of_baseChange_mvPolynomial.lean

